@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "gym-buddy Android App" {
  [Compose UI] as UI
  [Workout Session Controller] as Session
  [Camera Controller\n(CameraX)] as Camera
  [Frame Scheduler\nlatest-frame / backpressure] as Scheduler
  [Pose Perception\n(MediaPipe, bundled model)] as Pose
  [Coordinate Normalizer] as Normalize
  [Signal Processor\nSmoothing / velocity] as Signal
  [Tracking Quality Gate] as Quality
  [Exercise Analyzer\nIncline DB Press first] as Analyzer
  [Biomechanics Metrics] as Metrics
  [Deterministic Rule Engine\n+ Episode Tracker] as Rules
  [Cue Policy + Arbitrator] as CuePolicy
  [Live Overlay] as Overlay
  [Telemetry Sampler + Chunker\nbounded persistence rate] as TelemetryStage
  [Short-lived Telemetry Buffer\nbounded / best-effort] as TelemetryBuffer
  [Priority Persistence Queue\nbounded / reserved capacity] as PriorityQueue
  [Batch Writer\noff realtime path] as BatchWriter
  [Workout Repository] as Repo
  [Health Connect Adapter] as Health
  [Health Aggregator] as HealthAgg
  [Retention Worker\nstartup + periodic cleanup] as Retention
  [Startup Recovery] as Recovery
  [Room Database] as Room
}

UI --> Session : start/stop set
Session --> Repo : create/close workout hierarchy
Session --> Camera : start / stop accepting frames
Session --> Scheduler : await analysis quiescence on Stop Set
Session --> Analyzer : finalize partial/in-progress rep state
Session --> Rules : finalize active FormEvent episodes
Session --> PriorityQueue : SetCloseBarrier after finalization
Camera --> Scheduler : frames + timestamps
Scheduler --> Pose : newest eligible frame
Pose --> TelemetryStage : PoseObservation\n(no image bytes)
TelemetryStage --> TelemetryBuffer : versioned PoseObservationChunk
Pose --> Normalize : landmarks + confidence
Normalize --> Signal : canonical coordinates
Signal --> Quality : smoothed MovementFrame
Quality --> Analyzer : valid frames only
Quality --> Overlay : tracking/calibration guidance
Quality --> TelemetryBuffer : TrackingEvent on state changes
Analyzer --> Metrics : phase + movement features
Metrics --> Rules : metrics + phase + recent history
Rules --> CuePolicy : active actionable issue state
CuePolicy --> Overlay : highest-priority actionable cue
CuePolicy --> [Android TextToSpeech] : offline voice only; otherwise visual fallback

Analyzer --> PriorityQueue : completed/partial rep summary + CompactRepTrace
Metrics --> PriorityQueue : final rep metrics
Rules --> PriorityQueue : FormEvent activation/finalization + FormEvidence[]
CuePolicy --> PriorityQueue : CueDelivery when actually delivered
TelemetryBuffer --> BatchWriter : best-effort short-lived batches
PriorityQueue --> BatchWriter : priority batches first / SetCloseBarrier
BatchWriter --> Repo : persist / upsert transaction
Repo --> Room
BatchWriter --> Session : SetCloseBarrier commit ack
Session --> UI : set saved only after ack

Health --> HealthAgg : permitted Health Connect records
HealthAgg --> Repo : compact daily / weekly summaries only
Retention --> Repo : delete expired set telemetry/tracking data
Retention --> [App-private no-backup files] : delete expired debug media
Recovery --> Repo : stale ACTIVE -> INTERRUPTED on startup
UI --> Repo : history / workout state

note bottom of Pose
ML ends here. Everything downstream is deterministic code.
Pose model is bundled; no runtime network download.
PoseObservation contains pose output + frame transform metadata only,
never camera image bytes.
end note

note bottom of TelemetryStage
Realtime analysis FPS and persistence sampling rate are independent.
Persist only a bounded sample rate and chunk multiple observations
into versioned binary payloads to avoid one Room row per frame.
Exact sampling/chunk/codec policy belongs in SPEC/tests.
end note

note bottom of Session
At most one ExerciseSet is ACTIVE in the realtime pipeline.
Stop Set ordering is strict:
1) stop accepting new camera frames,
2) await in-flight analysis quiescence,
3) finalize analyzer/rule in-memory state,
4) enqueue SetCloseBarrier,
5) show saved/closed only after Room commit ack.
Raw short-lived telemetry need not block this barrier.
end note

note bottom of Rules
One continuous form problem is one stateful FormEvent episode.
PENDING stays in memory; ACTIVE/FINALIZED state is persisted using
the same event id so long-term data does not scale with frame rate.
end note

note bottom of TelemetryBuffer
Short-lived PoseObservationChunk / TrackingEvent data is best-effort.
Storage pressure may create gaps and must never block coaching.
end note

note bottom of PriorityQueue
This is an in-memory PRIORITY queue, not durable storage.
Durability begins only after Room commit.
Reserve control capacity for SetCloseBarrier and higher-value records.
end note

note bottom of Recovery
After process death, stale ACTIVE WorkoutSession /
ExerciseExecution / ExerciseSet / FormEvent records become INTERRUPTED.
end note

@enduml
